# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# Where the lead form POSTs its JSON payload. Point it at a CRM webhook, a form
# service, or a lead-capture API endpoint.
#
# Until this is set the form refuses to submit and tells the visitor to call
# instead — silently swallowing a real enquiry is worse than showing an error.
PUBLIC_LEAD_ENDPOINT=

# Google Maps Platform key. Used at BUILD TIME ONLY, by
# scripts/fetch-google-reviews.mjs, to pull the business's real Google reviews.
#
# Deliberately NOT prefixed PUBLIC_. Astro inlines every PUBLIC_* variable into
# the JavaScript it ships, so a key named PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY would be
# readable by anyone who opened the page source and billable to this account.
# Keep it unprefixed and it stays on the build machine.
#
# In CI this comes from the GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY repository secret. Locally, put
# it in .env (which is gitignored) only if you need to run `npm run reviews`;
# without it the build keeps the committed snapshot.
#
# Restrict the key in Google Cloud to the Places API. An unrestricted key found
# in a log or a screenshot can be spent against every API on the project.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
